From 71ce8b5dbbcb948b6a017022c06a374bf2f584f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Langsdorff <131063968+clangsdorff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:00:59 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 39/39] battery: keep the samsung battery cycle count

samsung battery drivers do not count cycles themselves. on stock the
framework adds the level drops up in /efs/FactoryApp/batt_discharge_level
and writes level / 100 to battery_cycle. the gsi never does, so the
driver keeps -1, the age based float voltage steps and the battery
health check never run, and battery information shows 0 cycles.

do the same on samsung vendors: keep adding level drops to the efs file,
write the cycle count to the driver and report it as the battery cycle
count. also pass the wear verdict from batt_misc_event in the battery
changed intent.
---
 .../com/android/server/BatteryService.java    |  22 +++
 .../android/server/SamsungBatteryCycle.java   | 136 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 158 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 services/core/java/com/android/server/SamsungBatteryCycle.java

